{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-09-Mar-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 34, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Prakash and Vinesh can complete a certain piece of work in 17 and 15 days, respectively, They started to work together, and after 4 days, Vinesh left. In how many days will Prakash complete the remaining work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A number when increased by 40 %', gives 3360. The number is:", "options": [{"text": "1200", "added": false}, {"text": "7200", "added": false}, {"text": "2400", "added": false}, {"text": "4800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "2400"}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "1/36"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A 338 m long train crosses a man walking at a speed of 6.8 km/h in the opposite direction in 12 seconds. What is the speed (in km/h) of the train ?", "options": [{"text": "94.6", "added": false}, {"text": "97.5", "added": false}, {"text": "90.5", "added": false}, {"text": "91.6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "94.6"}, {"n": 5, "text": "Pankaj and Kamal can do a piece of work in 12 days and 16 days, respectively. In how much time will they together complete the same work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A shopkeeper buys a watch for ₹2,000 and sells it for ₹2,400. What is the percentage of profit?", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "16.67%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "20%"}, {"n": 7, "text": "In a business, A, B and C invest ₹1,00,000, ₹2,00,000 and ₹2,50,000, respectively. If B gets ₹5,500 as profit, then the total profit (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "15,552", "added": false}, {"text": "15,125", "added": false}, {"text": "15,512", "added": false}, {"text": "15,215", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "15,125"}, {"n": 8, "text": "A dinner set is sold at ₹9,775 after giving a discount of 15%. What is the marked price of the dinner set?", "options": [{"text": "₹13,250", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12,250", "added": false}, {"text": "₹11,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹11,500"}, {"n": 9, "text": "If the length of cuboid is 2 cm, breadth is 7 cm and the volume of cuboid is 5278 cm3, then find the height of cuboid (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "377", "added": false}, {"text": "384", "added": false}, {"text": "372", "added": false}, {"text": "367", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "377"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Find the value of", "options": [{"text": "116", "added": false}, {"text": "107", "added": false}, {"text": "118", "added": false}, {"text": "110", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "110"}, {"n": 11, "text": "A sum of ₹5,000 is invested for 2 years at an annual interest rate of 6%. What will be the difference in the Compound Interest (CI) and Simple Interest (SI) at the end of 2 years? Use (1.06)2 = 1.1236", "options": [{"text": "₹28", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16", "added": false}, {"text": "₹18", "added": false}, {"text": "₹48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹18"}, {"n": 12, "text": "In a sale, a trader offers several discount schemes. Choose a scheme that provides the highest discount from the following options.", "options": [{"text": "Two successive discounts of 8% and 12%", "added": false}, {"text": "A single discount of 20%", "added": false}, {"text": "Two successive discounts of 10% and 11%", "added": false}, {"text": "Two successive discounts of 10% each", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "A single discount of 20%"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The sum of 8 numbers is 912. Find their average.", "options": [{"text": "112", "added": false}, {"text": "115", "added": false}, {"text": "114", "added": false}, {"text": "113", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "114"}, {"n": 14, "text": "A certain sum invested at 8% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, amounts to ₹10,580 at the end of 2 years. Find the sum.", "options": [{"text": "₹9,070.64", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,007.64", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,400.70", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,600.70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹9,070.64"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The smallest number which, when divided by 3, 5 and 7 leaves a remainder of 5 in each case, is:", "options": [{"text": "115", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "110", "added": false}, {"text": "95", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": "110"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The price of an